# Developer Documentation: Dev Framework Structure

✅ 1. GLOBAL INSTRUCTIONS: WHAT THEY ACTUALLY ARE

You nailed it. The global instructions file is:

Agnostic. Universal. No stack. No language. No tech.

It defines:

The existence of DevCycles

The existence of Artifacts

The relationships between them

The workflow

The expectations

The “contract” the whole framework runs on

It is NOT:

The place where you talk about Next.js

The place where you explain Prisma or Clerk

The place where features live

The place where tooling gets specific

This is the constitution, not the lawbooks.

We're aligned.

✅ 2. GLOBAL INSTRUCTIONS MUST LIST THE DEV CYCLES

Yes.
Only the names.
No details.
Just the canonical list so the framework knows the phases exist.

You want it to basically say:

“These are the DevCycle phases.
Instructions files define what they mean.”

We're aligned.

✅ 3. GLOBAL DEFINES THE ARTIFACT TYPES

You listed them perfectly:

Artifacts defined at global:

Prompts → they initiate cycles, point to instructions

Instructions → they define the DevCycle and point to toolset

Toolset → they define what tools the agent has access to

Settings/MCP/Extensions → these describe the environment

Profile → the combination of settings/extensions/MCP

Bootstrapper → detects + configures the profile and setup

Mode / Custom Agent → stack-specific behavior

PRD + TechReq → source of truth for requirements

Yes. This is the artifact taxonomy.
Global instructions define it.
Instructions implement it.

We’re aligned.

️‍🔥 4. GLOBAL MUST EXPLAIN THE WORKFLOW

Your bullets were perfect:

The workflow is:

Prompt initiates DevCycle

Prompt directs to specific Instructions

Instructions declare the Toolset

Agent uses instructions + toolset

Human stays in loop

Todo list updated from PRD/TechReq

Changelog updated with tasks completed

This is the universal workflow.

We're aligned.

🧑‍🤝‍🧑 5. HUMAN IN THE LOOP: YES

You want global instructions to mandate that:

Every dev cycle produces human-visible tasks

Tasks map to the PRD/TechReq

Tasks go into todo.md or GitHub issues

Tasks completed must be reflected in CHANGELOG

This is absolutely a global rule.

We're aligned.

